# CITATION.cff — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# `repository-code` and `doi` are deliberately absent. The repository has no remote
# configured yet, and a citation file that points at a URL nobody has published is worse
# than one that admits the URL is pending: a reader would follow it, find nothing, and
# reasonably distrust the rest of the metadata. Add them when the remote exists, and change
# nothing else here — every other field is true as written.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use QuantRisk++ in your research, please cite the software and the technical
  report. Every numerical claim in the report traces to an artifact hashed in
  evidence/manifest.json.
title: "QuantRisk++: A Reproducible C++/Python Engine for Stochastic Pricing, Monte Carlo Simulation, Portfolio Risk, Optimization and Stress Testing"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch C++20 numerical core with Python facades, covering Black-Scholes-Merton
  pricing, analytic and finite-difference Greeks, a Cox-Ross-Rubinstein lattice, Monte Carlo
  simulation with antithetic and control-variate variance reduction, Asian and barrier
  payoffs, Heston stochastic volatility, historical/Gaussian/Monte Carlo VaR and expected
  shortfall with bootstrap intervals, Kupiec and Christoffersen coverage backtests, three
  covariance estimators, six portfolio optimisers, and a scenario and stress layer with
  Euler attribution. Validation is the product: each component is checked against a closed
  form, a live independent oracle, or a statistical property measured over many
  replications, and 55 numbered limitations record where the claims stop.
authors:
  - name: Zhiren Xiao
    author-affiliation:
      name: School of Applied Statistics, Guangdong University of Finance
repository-code: https://github.com/Jackxiaozhiren/quantrisk-plus-plus
version: 1.5.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - quantitative-finance
  - monte-carlo
  - value-at-risk
  - expected-shortfall
  - portfolio-optimization
  - stress-testing
  - reproducibility
  - cxx20
